{"name":"Salt-N-Pepa","hex":"#dcd9db","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"salt","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A common substance, chemically consisting mainly of sodium chloride (NaCl), used extensively as a food ingredient, seasoning, condiment, and preservative.","One of the compounds formed from the reaction of an acid with a base, where a positive ion replaces a hydrogen of the acid."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of water: containing salt, saline.","Treated with salt as a preservative; cured with salt, salted."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salt"}],"entries":[{"title":"Salt-N-Pepa","blocks":[{"text":"Salt-N-Pepa is an American hip-hop group formed in New York City in 1985, that is composed of Salt, Pepa, and DJ Spinderella. Their debut album, Hot, Cool & Vicious (1986), sold more than 1 million copies in the US, making them the first female rap act to receive both a gold and platinum certification by the Recording Industry Association of America (RIAA). Its lead single, \"Push It\", which was released in 1987 as the B-side to their single \"Tramp\", peaked within the top 20 of the Billboard Hot 100."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Salt-n-Pepa_2013.jpg/330px-Salt-n-Pepa_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salt-N-Pepa","wikidata":"Q1545961"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Salt-N-Pepa_Jacket_-_Rock_and_Roll_Hall_of_Fame_%282014-12-30_13.14.38_by_Sam_Howzit%29.jpg/500px-Salt-N-Pepa_Jacket_-_Rock_and_Roll_Hall_of_Fame_%282014-12-30_13.14.38_by_Sam_Howzit%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Salt-N-Pepa_Jacket_-_Rock_and_Roll_Hall_of_Fame_%282014-12-30_13.14.38_by_Sam_Howzit%29.jpg/1280px-Salt-N-Pepa_Jacket_-_Rock_and_Roll_Hall_of_Fame_%282014